// Release-batch accounting guard: hold release-note publication while the host
// still counts merges nobody has written up. UNACCOUNTED_MERGE_COUNT is the
// number of merged pull requests in the canonical repository that no release
// candidate covers, counted by the host from a scan it has already declared
// complete.
// One is enough. A batch published with a single merge missing is a record
// that reads as complete and is not, and the next batch has no way to notice
// the gap because the merge is no longer recent.
// This rule gates release-note publication and nothing else. It must never be
// wired to a branch, a deploy, or an engineering merge: an unwritten changelog
// entry is a documentation debt, not a production risk.
// REGIME: all of them, but only over a completed scan. The count is only
// meaningful when aether_release_notes_coverage is satisfied; the two rules
// are deployed together and the coverage guard is what makes this one's zero
// mean something.
// CONDITIONS: the host counts from the scan result, and publishes no count at
// all when it has no scan - absence is the honest answer, and the evaluator
// turns an absent count into INPUT_UNAVAILABLE rather than into a calm zero.
// INVALIDATION: the outstanding merges being written up. The count falls back
// to zero and the rule stops proposing a hold, with no memory of having fired.
// SHAPE: 5m, matching the merge scan. The count cannot change faster than the
// scan that produces it.
// NOT aether_release_notes_uncovered_merge: that one observes a single merge
// landing without a candidate, one pull request at a time, and proposes no
// hold. This one is the batch-scope arithmetic and holds publication.
// CALIBRATED ON: a ceiling of one, which is policy rather than measurement and
// travels to any host that publishes release notes as batches. What does not
// travel is the definition of "covered" - which merges a release note is
// expected to mention is the publishing host's editorial rule.
strategy AetherReleaseNotesBatchUnaccounted {

    agent ReleaseDesk

    every 5m {

        if UNACCOUNTED_MERGE_COUNT >= 1 {

            pause()

        }

    }

}
